{"file":"Waves Exovian-3.1.9-v2.zip","bytes":490575,"status":"已读取","plugins":[{"path":".claude-plugin/plugin.json","name":"waves","description":"Product development framework for the AI agent era. Complete lifecycle: feasibility analysis with Monte Carlo/Bayesian projections, product foundation, blueprint creation, roadmaps, logbooks, and multi-session continuity. Replaces Scrum/Kanban with organic delivery cycles called waves.","version":"3.1.9","license":"AGPL-3.0-or-later","repository":"https://github.com/exovian-developments/waves","keywords":["framework","product-development","feasibility","blueprint","roadmap","logbook","monte-carlo","agile","waves","context","manifest","rules","protocol","multi-session"]}],"skills":[{"path":"skills/waves-protocol/SKILL.md","name":"waves-protocol","description":"This skill should be used when the user asks to \"initialize a project\", \"create a manifest\", \"create rules\", \"create a logbook\", \"update a manifest\", \"analyze project structure\", \"track development progress\", \"create a roadmap\", \"update roadmap\", \"analyze feasibility\", \"run feasibility analysis\", \"create a foundation\", \"create a blueprint\", \"product blueprint\", or needs guidance on structured context for AI agents. Also triggers for \"waves\", \"project context\", \"coding rules\", \"development logbook\", \"ticket resolution\", \"user preferences\", \"roadmap\", \"product roadmap\", \"phase planning\", \"feasibility\", \"monte carlo\", \"bayesian analysis\", \"product foundation\", \"product blueprint\", \"product lifecycle\", or any workflow involving project manifests, standards, product planning, or multi-session continuity.","headings":["waves Protocol","Core Concepts","Project Types Supported","File Structure","Directory-per-logbook convention (design_principle #11)","Correctness gate reviewers — input isolation (4 lenses)","Corpus mining — second-order metacognition (design_principle #11)","diverged_work — lightweight divergent work (